    <item>
      <title>GM’s Nasdaq Listing Won’t Solve Its Valuation Challenge</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-27/gm-s-nasdaq-listing-won-t-solve-its-valuation-challenge</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">1aa18280b1687fd0f2d23b42</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:14:57 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Automakers are “technology” companies on a purely semantic level: The internal combustion engine is one of a select few inventions that truly define modern life. It also dates back to the 19th century, so automakers are not, by and large, regarded as technology stocks. General Motors Co. seems set on changing the wisdom of the crowd on this. Its latest step in that direction involves relocating from the New York Stock Exchange to Nasdaq, with its silicon-inflected aura.</description>
      <dc:creator>Liam Denning</dc:creator>
